// EXPECT: element 0 of a word[] literal is a string
// EXPECT-IDCPY: list element has type int, expected string
// docs/FRICTION.md 8. The primary compiler takes the literal's type from the
// slot it is going into, so the string is element 0 of a word[] and is named
// as such. idc.py takes it from element 0, so it decides the literal is a
// string[] and reports the 0 in element 1 instead. Both refuse the program.
main() {
  word[] xs = ["nope", 0];
  print(len(xs));
} return int 0;
